<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n76904" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾰλίμ-φημος</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾰλίμ-φᾱμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>back-speaking, recanting</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π.
				ἀοιδά,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παλινῳδία</span>
			, a song <i>of recantation</i>, reproaching the male sex
			instead of the female, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				1096
			</span></i> (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Med.</u>
				415
			</span></i> sq. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακόφημος, δύσφημος,
					λαβροσύναι</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Tryph.
				423
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. εὐχαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.301
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄναρ</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				55
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
